1
00:00:01,830 --> 00:00:04,200
A party?

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:09,120
There's a party to celebrate the 
appointment of a new Highlander emissary,

3
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:12,780
and they've asked that 
you and Rafinha attend.

4
00:00:13,050 --> 00:00:16,620
It was Brother Raf who 
sent that message, right?

5
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:19,260
But why us?

6
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:24,050
He said if I told you to bring Lyn, 
you'd understand.

7
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:26,010
What does that mean?

8
00:00:26,010 --> 00:00:27,750
I don't know...

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,440
Um, why am I here?

10
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:35,470
Because you're going to the party too.

11
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:43,170
Liselotte's father, the chancellor, 
will also be in attendance.

12
00:00:43,170 --> 00:00:47,550
I told him I'm bringing a friend.

13
00:00:47,550 --> 00:00:51,020
B-But I...

14
00:00:51,490 --> 00:00:53,860
Come with us, Leone!

15
00:00:57,630 --> 00:00:59,110
Okay.

16
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:01,700
Thanks, Liselotte.

17
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:05,820
Okay, next stop: shopping for party dresses!

18
00:01:21,050 --> 00:01:24,020
<u>Reborn</u>

19
00:01:21,050 --> 00:01:24,020
to Master the Blade
     From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

20
00:01:21,050 --> 00:01:24,020
to Master the Blade
From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

21
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:40,080
If we're going to a party, 
we'll need dresses!

22
00:02:40,170 --> 00:02:45,140
Episode 7    The Hyral Menas's Disease

23
00:02:40,440 --> 00:02:45,290
You don't need to buy a dress for me too...

24
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:46,910
It's fine!

25
00:02:46,910 --> 00:02:50,300
Brother Raf will pay for it all!

26
00:02:50,620 --> 00:02:52,470
Sounds good to me.

27
00:02:52,470 --> 00:02:53,980
Magicite beasts!

28
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:04,860
Eris!

29
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,640
You guys...

30
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:07,880
Where are the magicite beasts?

31
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:11,340
It's fine. I defeated them all.

32
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:13,950
Is that... a humanoid?

33
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:16,400
Does that mean it used to be a Highlander?

34
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:19,730
No, it was a demihuman magicite beast.

35
00:03:19,730 --> 00:03:22,310
Demihumans are affected by the Prism Flow.

36
00:03:23,050 --> 00:03:26,140
But I'm a Hyral Menas, so I'm fine.

37
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:29,880
Um, Ripple... are you all right?

38
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:31,480
You look kind of unwell.

39
00:03:32,190 --> 00:03:34,330
I'm fine, I'm fine.

40
00:03:34,330 --> 00:03:37,320
Just a little dizzy. I'm feeling just fine!

41
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:41,420
The same thing happened last time, though.

42
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:42,390
Last time?

43
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:46,360
We've been through this several times 
since returning to the capital.

44
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:49,820
We've seen magicite beasts 
appear out of nowhere.

45
00:03:50,110 --> 00:03:52,870
And then Ripple ends up feeling sick.

46
00:03:52,870 --> 00:03:54,720
I don't know why.

47
00:03:55,650 --> 00:03:59,030
I'll be just fine soon. It's okay.

48
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:04,260
You think it's the Bloodchain Brigade that 
are making the magicite beasts appear?

49
00:04:04,260 --> 00:04:06,280
I don't know.

50
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:09,730
We'll have to have the new 
emissary look into it.

51
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:14,660
What's this?

52
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:16,710
The money for tailoring your dresses.

53
00:04:16,710 --> 00:04:20,550
Rafael had a sudden mission to deal with, 
so he couldn't come.

54
00:04:20,550 --> 00:04:23,920
That's why we came to give you this instead.

55
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:26,840
Thank you!

56
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:28,370
Thanks for coming all this way!

57
00:04:28,370 --> 00:04:34,050
It's fine! But in exchange, 
let us come shopping with you.

58
00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:37,130
Several Days Later

59
00:04:37,510 --> 00:04:39,490
We're almost out of time.

60
00:04:39,490 --> 00:04:41,030
Will you need much longer?

61
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:42,450
All set!

62
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:47,000
You look great!

63
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,510
You're gorgeous!

64
00:04:48,510 --> 00:04:51,310
This is great! It's fantastic!

65
00:04:52,990 --> 00:04:54,250
Yup.

66
00:04:54,250 --> 00:04:58,310
I like how cute you are when 
you get excited over yourself!

67
00:04:58,570 --> 00:05:00,570
That's rare...

68
00:05:01,790 --> 00:05:03,740
I'm hungry.

69
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:04,830
That's right.

70
00:05:04,830 --> 00:05:08,730
We wanted to leave room for all the good food
at the party, so we haven't eaten anything...

71
00:05:10,150 --> 00:05:11,700
Negotiations?

72
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:15,910
Yes. To see if we can get 
the latest equipment.

73
00:05:16,460 --> 00:05:20,630
It's a good chance to ask 
the emissary directly.

74
00:05:20,630 --> 00:05:24,580
But will they say yes, you think?

75
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:28,840
I actually know the emissary.

76
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:32,340
I stayed with him when I was on 
an exchange program in the Highland.

77
00:05:32,610 --> 00:05:34,520
An exchange program in the Highland?

78
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:36,690
I had no idea there was such a thing!

79
00:05:36,690 --> 00:05:39,550
It was somewhat of a special case.

80
00:05:39,550 --> 00:05:44,770
When Prince Wein was there on exchange, 
I went as his bodyguard.

81
00:05:44,770 --> 00:05:48,340
Ma'am, would you ask the emissary

82
00:05:48,340 --> 00:05:52,000
if he has any information 
on the Bloodchain Brigade?

83
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:59,950
Yeah, he might know something.

84
00:05:59,950 --> 00:06:03,210
<i>And it'd be great if he knew anything 
about the man in the black mask.</i>

85
00:06:04,140 --> 00:06:06,510
That could be difficult.

86
00:06:06,510 --> 00:06:08,800
He might be willing to talk to the knights,

87
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:13,390
but not to a bunch of academy students.

88
00:06:14,070 --> 00:06:17,100
Oh... Yeah, that's right.

89
00:06:17,430 --> 00:06:21,090
Let's find information on the 
Bloodchain Brigade ourselves.

90
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:23,440
I'll help.

91
00:06:23,770 --> 00:06:25,710
We mustn't rush things carelessly.

92
00:06:25,710 --> 00:06:28,310
Thanks, everyone.

93
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:33,890
I'm so hungry!

94
00:06:33,890 --> 00:06:35,720
Let's hurry up and go inside, Chris!

95
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:38,230
Rani, if you run in that dress...

96
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:39,780
You'll trip.

97
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:42,770
Why didn't you say so sooner?

98
00:06:42,770 --> 00:06:44,020
You okay?

99
00:06:47,890 --> 00:06:49,110
Are you hurt?

100
00:06:49,110 --> 00:06:51,650
You mustn't cause trouble for Chris.

101
00:06:52,290 --> 00:06:53,630
Brother!

102
00:06:53,910 --> 00:06:56,680
Chris, I'm sorry she's such a handful.

103
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:58,670
Thanks for always being there for her...

104
00:06:59,510 --> 00:07:02,380
Not at all. She's always 
been there for me, too.

105
00:07:03,950 --> 00:07:06,340
Is something wrong, Cousin?

106
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:10,400
I was just thinking that this is the 
first time I've seen you in a dress.

107
00:07:11,150 --> 00:07:12,910
You're really pretty.

108
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:15,140
Thank you.

109
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:17,440
Rani helped me out.

110
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:18,630
Right?

111
00:07:18,900 --> 00:07:21,830
I'm pretty confident in my choice this time!

112
00:07:21,830 --> 00:07:26,770
And um... I guess you brought Lyn, too.

113
00:07:27,270 --> 00:07:31,050
Oh! Brother, you were just 
looking at her breasts!

114
00:07:27,410 --> 00:07:30,740
<i>I know it's just something men 
instinctively do around women,</i>

115
00:07:30,740 --> 00:07:34,390
<i>but to be honest, being looked at that way...</i>

116
00:07:31,050 --> 00:07:34,390
S-Sorry! I was just wondering 
where Lyn was...

117
00:07:35,570 --> 00:07:37,690
What's wrong?

118
00:07:37,690 --> 00:07:41,880
We're hungry. We haven't eaten all day.

119
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:44,600
We heard we could get good food here.

120
00:07:45,210 --> 00:07:49,060
Then let's talk later. Shall we head inside?

121
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:50,770
Let's!

122
00:07:51,410 --> 00:07:54,600
Yes, please take them inside, Sir Rafael.

123
00:07:54,600 --> 00:08:00,280
The noise is so loud that the guests 
might think <i>all</i> of us are starving.

124
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:05,140
I'll go say hello to my father...

125
00:08:05,140 --> 00:08:06,420
Bye!

126
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:08,000
See you later!

127
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:13,460
Did you see that girl? She's gorgeous!

128
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:17,210
She's as pretty as a doll... 
I can't take my eyes off her!

129
00:08:19,250 --> 00:08:20,390
Wh-What?

130
00:08:20,390 --> 00:08:21,770
Their stomachs are growling?

131
00:08:23,430 --> 00:08:27,850
Sorry! I've been so busy 
that I haven't had time to eat!

132
00:08:27,850 --> 00:08:31,060
Brother's so nice! I love him!

133
00:08:31,060 --> 00:08:33,450
Thank you, my dear cousin!

134
00:08:34,060 --> 00:08:36,040
Okay, go ahead and eat!

135
00:08:36,040 --> 00:08:37,510
Yes!

136
00:08:37,510 --> 00:08:38,990
Chris, let's eat!

137
00:08:38,990 --> 00:08:39,950
Yes, let's!

138
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:45,450
Magicite beasts? Here?!

139
00:08:47,190 --> 00:08:49,090
My meat!

140
00:08:49,090 --> 00:08:50,500
What a surprise!

141
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:53,340
No fair, Chris!

142
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:56,180
Don't worry, I got you some too.

143
00:08:56,180 --> 00:08:57,760
When did she...

144
00:08:59,550 --> 00:09:01,140
Way to go, Chris!

145
00:09:01,410 --> 00:09:03,560
Some of the tables are still intact.

146
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:05,450
Let's fight to protect our food!

147
00:09:06,260 --> 00:09:09,190
Protect the people, not the food!

148
00:09:09,190 --> 00:09:11,570
Well, it's all the same in the end, right?

149
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:15,620
Aether Pierce!

150
00:09:15,620 --> 00:09:17,210
Chris, get back!

151
00:09:17,210 --> 00:09:18,410
<i>He's fast.</i>

152
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:26,380
<i>His strength, speed, and technique...</i>

153
00:09:26,380 --> 00:09:28,510
<i>They're all on an entirely different level.</i>

154
00:09:28,510 --> 00:09:30,830
<i>He's been no slouch 
when it comes to practicing!</i>

155
00:09:31,510 --> 00:09:32,790
I hope you're all unharmed?

156
00:09:32,790 --> 00:09:34,870
Wow, Brother!

157
00:09:34,870 --> 00:09:38,780
You're the only person besides Chris 
who moves too fast for me to see!

158
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:42,170
That slash on the fifth attack 
and thrust on the seventeenth

159
00:09:42,170 --> 00:09:44,800
were especially well executed, Cousin Raf!

160
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:47,440
You saw the whole thing, Inglis?

161
00:09:47,440 --> 00:09:49,900
Yup! There were twenty-one attacks in all!

162
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:52,620
Hey, how many did you see, Rafinha?

163
00:09:50,270 --> 00:09:53,860
Maybe you didn't need my help.

164
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:54,590
Just the first two or three.

165
00:09:53,860 --> 00:09:56,490
It's just habit, though, you know.

166
00:09:54,590 --> 00:09:56,480
I'm glad it's not just me.

167
00:09:56,730 --> 00:09:59,830
No, it was wonderful to see!

168
00:09:59,830 --> 00:10:02,200
I'd love to challenge you to a duel soon!

169
00:10:02,470 --> 00:10:03,530
Holding nothing back!

170
00:10:03,530 --> 00:10:07,330
Well, I wouldn't want you to get hurt...

171
00:10:07,330 --> 00:10:09,250
I guess we could do a 
practice fight, though...

172
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:12,700
<i>What would get him to fight me 
at full strength?</i>

173
00:10:13,050 --> 00:10:16,160
Rafael, leave this room to them,

174
00:10:16,160 --> 00:10:19,130
and hurry to Prince Wein 
and Emissary Theodore!

175
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:22,590
All right.

176
00:10:22,990 --> 00:10:26,900
Rani, Chris, Leone. 
Keep the people here safe.

177
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:28,700
Okay, Brother!

178
00:10:28,700 --> 00:10:30,090
Got it!

179
00:10:30,090 --> 00:10:31,520
Leave it to us!

180
00:10:33,190 --> 00:10:34,940
Here you go, everyone.

181
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:37,180
I was looking forward to 
wearing these dresses,

182
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:39,330
but I guess we're doing the 
same thing we always do.

183
00:10:39,330 --> 00:10:43,770
No kidding. They could've let us have 
the day off to have some fun...

184
00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:49,140
I <i>am</i> having fun! 
I love fighting magicite beasts!

185
00:10:49,140 --> 00:10:53,380
Chris is special! 
She's a wild animal in a dress!

186
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:56,080
That's right!

187
00:10:56,080 --> 00:11:02,050
How rude. I'm going 
to fight elegantly today.

188
00:10:56,550 --> 00:10:59,190
<i>Is the fact that they're not scared 
in a situation like this</i>

189
00:10:59,190 --> 00:11:01,810
<i>a sign that they'll make good knights?</i>

190
00:11:04,510 --> 00:11:06,180
Like a proper lady.

191
00:11:06,730 --> 00:11:07,760
Observe!

192
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:20,530
See? Very elegant!

193
00:11:20,530 --> 00:11:22,790
Yes, but...

194
00:11:22,790 --> 00:11:26,590
You're taking them down so easily that 
you're actually more scary than usual.

195
00:11:26,590 --> 00:11:28,680
Yes, it's a little too easy.

196
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:31,100
But I don't want to mess up my dress.

197
00:11:31,100 --> 00:11:34,590
Oh, you guys finish them off.

198
00:11:34,590 --> 00:11:35,820
I know!

199
00:11:36,830 --> 00:11:38,480
Chris! They're coming!

200
00:11:39,250 --> 00:11:40,860
From over here, too!

201
00:11:40,860 --> 00:11:41,920
They're fast!

202
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:49,610
<i>I suppose one finger is too slow.</i>

203
00:11:50,700 --> 00:11:51,570
<i>In which case...</i>

204
00:11:55,740 --> 00:11:57,700
Yes! It worked!

205
00:11:57,700 --> 00:11:59,760
What? With both hands?!

206
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:01,140
Check this out, Rani!

207
00:12:14,930 --> 00:12:16,920
That was a good fight, huh?

208
00:12:17,990 --> 00:12:20,760
I'm glad you had fun!

209
00:12:20,760 --> 00:12:23,300
I was enjoying myself so much, 
I went a little overboard.

210
00:12:23,300 --> 00:12:25,390
It was more than a little, I thought.

211
00:12:25,390 --> 00:12:30,310
Ma'am, we beat the magicite beasts, 
which means we can eat now, right?

212
00:12:30,310 --> 00:12:31,830
Right?

213
00:12:31,830 --> 00:12:34,350
You two...

214
00:12:34,580 --> 00:12:36,970
Sure, in moderation.

215
00:12:36,970 --> 00:12:42,330
I'll go finish them off while 
you replenish your strength.

216
00:12:42,330 --> 00:12:44,300
Thank you!

217
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:47,680
Leone! Principal Miliera!

218
00:12:48,530 --> 00:12:50,090
You're safe!

219
00:12:50,090 --> 00:12:52,610
Yes. So's my father.

220
00:12:53,740 --> 00:12:54,870
But...

221
00:12:55,410 --> 00:12:56,570
Huh?

222
00:12:56,570 --> 00:12:59,250
Where are Inglis and Rafinha?

223
00:12:59,710 --> 00:13:01,550
Oh, it's Liselotte!

224
00:13:01,750 --> 00:13:03,340
Hey there!

225
00:13:03,340 --> 00:13:06,340
I have no idea what you're saying.

226
00:13:06,340 --> 00:13:08,590
Anyway, come with me!

227
00:13:08,590 --> 00:13:11,050
Something's wrong with Ripple.

228
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:21,390
Brother Rafael!

229
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:24,170
Looks like you finished up.

230
00:13:24,170 --> 00:13:26,810
Which means our only remaining problem is...

231
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:32,830
What is that?

232
00:13:32,830 --> 00:13:34,530
The space around her is distorted?

233
00:13:34,530 --> 00:13:38,330
Is that awful-looking light what 
summoned the magicite beasts?

234
00:13:38,330 --> 00:13:41,030
Yes, she suddenly collapsed, and...

235
00:13:49,580 --> 00:13:52,720
We defeated the magicite beasts, 
but I don't know what's going on...

236
00:13:52,990 --> 00:13:58,430
So that Hyral Menas summoned 
magicite beasts to make them attack us!

237
00:13:58,430 --> 00:14:01,740
No, Ripple wouldn't do that!

238
00:14:01,740 --> 00:14:03,960
Eris and the other Hyral Menases

239
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:07,520
have worked so hard to protect 
this country and its people!

240
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:10,500
You can't trust them, even after that?

241
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:13,880
Of course, we know that.

242
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:15,450
You're right, but...

243
00:14:18,150 --> 00:14:19,850
Don't be angry at them.

244
00:14:19,850 --> 00:14:24,230
They have a duty to be ready for danger.

245
00:14:24,230 --> 00:14:26,010
O-Okay...

246
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:30,590
Any idea what could have 
caused this, Theodore?

247
00:14:30,640 --> 00:14:34,640
Highland Emissary Theodore

248
00:14:30,950 --> 00:14:36,310
It's hard to say for sure, 
but it may be the Hierarchy.

249
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:38,490
The Hierarchy?

250
00:14:38,490 --> 00:14:41,510
There are two factions of Highlanders.

251
00:14:41,970 --> 00:14:43,850
One is the Grand Duchy.

252
00:14:43,850 --> 00:14:49,860
They give us not only Artifacts, but also 
Flying Gears and other new technology.

253
00:14:50,290 --> 00:14:52,500
The other is the Hierarchy.

254
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:59,280
They prefer to keep new technology from 
those of us on the surface whenever possible.

255
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:02,020
Each of these two large factions

256
00:15:02,020 --> 00:15:07,770
would send Hyral Menases to each country 
to maintain the balance of power.

257
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:11,290
But that balance is collapsing.

258
00:15:11,630 --> 00:15:14,830
Ripple is a Hyral Menas 
created by the Hierarchy.

259
00:15:14,830 --> 00:15:18,260
They may have prepared a way 
to destroy her from within.

260
00:15:18,530 --> 00:15:22,930
So Ripple's just a toy 
in your power struggles?

261
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:25,140
Eris...

262
00:15:26,670 --> 00:15:31,120
She offered herself up to become a 
Hyral Menas and protect the surface.

263
00:15:31,510 --> 00:15:32,820
But...

264
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:36,370
the Highland... the Highlanders... 
are doing this to her?

265
00:15:36,890 --> 00:15:39,590
Why are we even here?

266
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:44,330
To protect, I think.

267
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:47,460
You protected me.

268
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:50,680
And I'm glad we have the Flying Gears, too!

269
00:15:50,970 --> 00:15:53,770
We can get to people who are far away faster

270
00:15:53,770 --> 00:15:56,490
and protect them from the magicite beasts!

271
00:15:56,490 --> 00:15:57,890
You...

272
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:06,260
Rafinha's right, isn't she, Inglis?

273
00:16:06,260 --> 00:16:09,530
Yes. I like it that way, 
because I get to fight more.

274
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:12,870
No, that's not what I meant...

275
00:16:13,140 --> 00:16:15,950
I'm sorry for speaking out of turn.

276
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:21,050
No, it's better to think the way that you do.

277
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:26,720
I'll do my best to bring 
Ripple back to normal.

278
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:28,790
Thank you.

279
00:16:29,330 --> 00:16:31,430
And I need to thank you, too.

280
00:16:32,040 --> 00:16:35,720
For speaking up back there. Thank you.

281
00:16:37,350 --> 00:16:38,170
Of course!

282
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:40,880
It was a pure-hearted and honest opinion.

283
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:44,850
You're not only beautiful on the outside, 
but you have a beautiful heart, too.

284
00:16:44,850 --> 00:16:46,520
N-No, I...

285
00:16:47,630 --> 00:16:49,300
"Beautiful?"

286
00:16:49,650 --> 00:16:52,320
<i>I've never seen Rani like this before.</i>

287
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:56,500
<i>Perhaps I've finally found 
the boy I need to drive off!</i>

288
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:57,660
Would you tell me your name?

289
00:16:57,660 --> 00:16:59,490
This is Rafinha Bilford.

290
00:16:59,490 --> 00:17:03,450
The younger sister of 
Holy Knight Rafael over there.

291
00:17:03,890 --> 00:17:06,540
I'm Inglis Eucus, her squire.

292
00:17:06,540 --> 00:17:09,590
Hey, Chris! What's gotten into you?

293
00:17:09,590 --> 00:17:11,800
I'm just doing what a squire should!

294
00:17:12,080 --> 00:17:15,040
Rafinha? Inglis?

295
00:17:15,650 --> 00:17:19,890
So you're the ones who 
saved my little sister?

296
00:17:19,890 --> 00:17:21,020
Sister?

297
00:17:21,020 --> 00:17:23,970
Seilyn is my little sister.

298
00:17:27,570 --> 00:17:30,930
I heard she was turned 
into a magicite beast.

299
00:17:30,930 --> 00:17:32,160
Where is she now?

300
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:33,640
Right here.

301
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:37,650
Seilyn?

302
00:17:38,840 --> 00:17:42,780
It's small, but yes, I can feel her mana.

303
00:17:43,060 --> 00:17:48,760
I'm sorry. All we could do 
was save her in this state.

304
00:17:49,070 --> 00:17:52,430
No, you did well.

305
00:17:52,430 --> 00:17:55,730
I'll find a way to turn her back.

306
00:17:55,730 --> 00:17:57,630
Theodore...

307
00:17:57,630 --> 00:18:00,240
I'll take her, then.

308
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:01,170
Of course.

309
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:06,610
Seilyn, you're safe now!

310
00:18:08,890 --> 00:18:10,190
Ouch!

311
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:12,990
What's wrong, Seilyn?

312
00:18:19,230 --> 00:18:23,030
Lyn, your brother's here for you!

313
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:29,640
Lyn, that tickles!

314
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:33,570
Chris, don't move. I'll pull her out!

315
00:18:33,570 --> 00:18:36,090
No! Rani!

316
00:18:37,140 --> 00:18:39,550
Maybe she doesn't want to go back?

317
00:18:39,550 --> 00:18:42,760
It feels like she's different 
from the Seilyn I knew.

318
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:47,110
Maybe I should leave her 
in your care for now.

319
00:18:47,110 --> 00:18:48,450
All right.

320
00:18:48,450 --> 00:18:50,850
That's fine with us.

321
00:18:51,130 --> 00:18:53,550
Theodore, Ripple has...

322
00:18:54,250 --> 00:18:56,070
She's awake?!

323
00:19:04,190 --> 00:19:05,770
Whew...

324
00:19:05,770 --> 00:19:07,070
Are you okay?

325
00:19:07,470 --> 00:19:08,770
For now.

326
00:19:09,290 --> 00:19:12,780
But I remember what happened, a little.

327
00:19:13,390 --> 00:19:16,520
I hurt everyone... I'm sorry.

328
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:18,500
It's not your fault.

329
00:19:18,500 --> 00:19:20,040
That's right.

330
00:19:20,040 --> 00:19:21,900
Thanks, you guys.

331
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:24,750
But I can't take this anymore...

332
00:19:25,410 --> 00:19:28,300
I'm not sure why I even 
became a Hyral Menas.

333
00:19:28,970 --> 00:19:34,650
Listen, Wein. If you can't find a way 
to stop this, go ahead and destroy me.

334
00:19:34,940 --> 00:19:38,470
Or throw me away somewhere 
where nobody else is around.

335
00:19:38,980 --> 00:19:40,200
Never!

336
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:44,160
We could never do that to the 
woman who protects our country!

337
00:19:45,050 --> 00:19:46,770
This won't go on for much longer.

338
00:19:46,770 --> 00:19:50,840
Just rest someplace that's well guarded.

339
00:19:53,260 --> 00:19:56,970
I'll find a place for her right away. 
And I'll post guards to protect her.

340
00:19:57,710 --> 00:19:58,540
Thanks.

341
00:19:58,850 --> 00:20:00,160
Excuse me.

342
00:20:00,570 --> 00:20:03,190
I have a suggestion...

343
00:20:03,190 --> 00:20:05,270
Go ahead and say it.

344
00:20:05,270 --> 00:20:08,980
Why not bring her to the knights' academy?

345
00:20:09,810 --> 00:20:11,770
The knights' academy?

346
00:20:11,770 --> 00:20:16,450
Losing Ripple will already be 
a big hit to the knights' strength.

347
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:22,470
And if you have to assign people 
to guard her, you'll lose even more strength.

348
00:20:22,470 --> 00:20:24,400
That should be avoided, I think.

349
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:30,670
So we have someone besides the knights 
protect her, to help keep the nation safe?

350
00:20:30,670 --> 00:20:32,840
That's a great idea, Chris!

351
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:35,740
We can keep Ripple safe ourselves!

352
00:20:35,740 --> 00:20:37,280
I'm against this.

353
00:20:38,340 --> 00:20:40,670
The academy is in the middle of a city.

354
00:20:41,090 --> 00:20:45,290
If the magicite beasts get out, it will 
put the people of the capital in danger.

355
00:20:46,060 --> 00:20:48,280
If I may speak, too...

356
00:20:48,810 --> 00:20:54,850
If we want to find out why this happened, 
we'll need Miliera's help.

357
00:20:54,850 --> 00:20:56,300
Which means...

358
00:20:56,300 --> 00:21:01,510
It would be best to have her at the academy, 
where my lab is located.

359
00:21:05,220 --> 00:21:08,550
Ripple is feeling guilty right now.

360
00:21:08,550 --> 00:21:12,370
So we'll defeat all the 
magicite beasts she summons

361
00:21:12,370 --> 00:21:17,590
without any of us getting hurt 
or putting the townspeople in danger.

362
00:21:17,590 --> 00:21:20,410
Then she won't feel so bad.

363
00:21:20,410 --> 00:21:23,800
I want to protect her heart, as well.

364
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:27,000
Inglis...

365
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:28,870
I like that!

366
00:21:28,870 --> 00:21:31,330
"Protect her heart!"

367
00:21:32,230 --> 00:21:33,480
Thanks...

368
00:21:33,850 --> 00:21:36,930
I've decided to put my faith in your resolve

369
00:21:37,340 --> 00:21:40,060
and leave her in the academy's care.

370
00:21:40,440 --> 00:21:42,690
Miliera, I entrust the rest to you.

371
00:21:42,690 --> 00:21:43,910
Of course, Your Highness.

372
00:21:44,370 --> 00:21:46,940
Theodore, please do what you can 
to assist them, too.

373
00:21:46,940 --> 00:21:49,370
We'll get to the bottom of this. I promise.

374
00:21:49,670 --> 00:21:51,830
Thanks, everyone.

375
00:21:52,110 --> 00:21:52,940
Right!

376
00:21:53,770 --> 00:21:57,490
I didn't realize Inglis cared so much.

377
00:21:57,490 --> 00:22:00,490
You're always seeing the best in people, huh?

378
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:05,850
Being around Ripple will give her 
more chances to fight magicite beasts.

379
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:08,090
You don't think that's what she was thinking?

380
00:22:09,510 --> 00:22:12,010
Maybe that's it...

381
